>> title: Mujaddara
>> category: Rice, Beans & Grains
>> tags: lentils, rice, levantine, vegetarian, stovetop
>> servings: 6
>> time: 1 hr 15 min
>> step.1: simmer 15 min, drain
>> step.2: fry 25 min
>> step.3: fry crisp 25 min, drain
>> step.4: toast 2 min
>> step.5: simmer covered 20 min
>> step.6: rest 10 min, fluff, scatter on top

Simmer @brown lentils{1%cup}(200 g; rinsed) in @water{3%cups}(710 mL) for ~{15%min}, until half-tender, then drain.

Fry @yellow onions{2%large}(500 g; thinly sliced) in @olive oil{1/3%cup}(80 mL) in a #skillet{} until deep brown and sweet, ~{25%min}.

Fry @yellow onions{2%large}(500 g; thinly sliced, for the top) in @olive oil{1/3%cup}(80 mL) in a #skillet{} until dark and crisp, ~{25%min}, then lift onto paper towels to drain.

Toast @basmati rice{1%cup}(200 g; rinsed) with @ground cumin{1 1/2%tsp}, @ground coriander{1%tsp}, and @ground allspice{1/2%tsp} in @&(~2)fried onions{} for ~{2%min}.

Simmer @&(~1)rice{} covered over low heat for ~{20%min} with @&(~4)lentils{}, @hot water{1 3/4%cups}(415 mL), and @kosher salt{1 1/2%tsp}.

Rest @&(~1)pot{} off the heat for ~{10%min}, then fluff with a #fork{}, fold in @flat-leaf parsley{1/4%cup}, and scatter @&(~3)crisp onions{} over the top.
